WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:00.903
- Hey guys, How's it going?

00:00:00.903 --> 00:00:03.344
Today we're gonna be unboxing
the new Nintendo Switch,

00:00:03.344 --> 00:00:04.816
it comes out on March third.

00:00:04.816 --> 00:00:06.947
So a huge thank you to
Nintendo for sending me

00:00:06.947 --> 00:00:11.460
an early advanced console and
I am so incredibly grateful,

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.121
so thank you guys so much.

00:00:13.121 --> 00:00:16.179
Let's get into the unboxing, now.

00:00:16.179 --> 00:00:18.295
(knife clicks)

00:00:18.295 --> 00:00:20.918
I already started cutting into it.

00:00:20.918 --> 00:00:23.348
Oh, never ever cut towards yourself,

00:00:23.348 --> 00:00:27.181
especially with this
ridiculously sharp knife.

00:00:28.313 --> 00:00:29.436
(groans)

00:00:29.436 --> 00:00:30.686
I'm so excited!

00:00:32.952 --> 00:00:37.142
There's Zelda Amiibo,
I'm so freaking excited!

00:00:37.142 --> 00:00:39.242
I've been meaning for the
longest time to do an entire

00:00:39.242 --> 00:00:42.081
Amiibo collection because
I have almost all of them.

00:00:42.081 --> 00:00:43.541
So one of these days soon, look for that,

00:00:43.541 --> 00:00:47.541
but right now let's
just...(breathless exclamation)

00:00:47.541 --> 00:00:51.129
This is probably one of
the most incredible Amiibo

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:54.656
that I've ever seen, it's the Guardian.

00:00:54.656 --> 00:00:57.156
Zelda, oh she looks so pretty.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.683
Oh boy! Here he is!

00:01:02.578 --> 00:01:04.578
Sweet, beautiful Switch.

00:01:05.854 --> 00:01:08.812
Look how cute this
little, tiny cartridge is.

00:01:08.812 --> 00:01:11.479
It's like the size of my Iphone.

00:01:12.399 --> 00:01:13.982
Time to open it up!

00:01:15.698 --> 00:01:18.229
Oh my. You're beautiful.

00:01:18.229 --> 00:01:20.690
I am so excited, this is the neon version.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:24.273
We've got our two
Joy-Con controllers here.

00:01:27.678 --> 00:01:30.313
It seems way more neon than
the New York event I went to

00:01:30.313 --> 00:01:33.737
because the coloring in
that event was so bright,

00:01:33.737 --> 00:01:35.272
that you actually didn't get a good chance

00:01:35.272 --> 00:01:37.472
to really check out the colors of these.

00:01:37.472 --> 00:01:39.347
Oh it feels good. (clicking)

00:01:39.347 --> 00:01:41.763
(upbeat music)

00:01:41.763 --> 00:01:44.059
(chuckles) There we go, switch 'em around!

00:01:44.059 --> 00:01:45.579
Switch 'em around, did you get it?

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:47.329
Did you get the joke?

00:01:48.754 --> 00:01:52.087
Look at this, this is the Switch itself.

00:01:58.099 --> 00:02:02.380
I'm gonna get this so smudgy
and like point five seconds.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:03.797
Lift off the top.

00:02:05.398 --> 00:02:08.815
More items, we've got our Joy-Con straps!

00:02:14.401 --> 00:02:16.401
Let's put these in here.

00:02:18.486 --> 00:02:19.371
Let's put the next side in,

00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:21.846
so there's a little
tiny groove right here,

00:02:21.846 --> 00:02:26.408
and you just slide this
right in just like this.

00:02:26.408 --> 00:02:29.177
This looks so cool, I
absolutely love these colors.

00:02:29.177 --> 00:02:32.202
I think I'm gonna go get
a manicure this color.

00:02:32.202 --> 00:02:35.791
So we got controller, we
got our Switch screen,

00:02:35.791 --> 00:02:37.708
we've got a HDMI cable.

00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:40.512
You know what that looks like,

00:02:40.512 --> 00:02:42.012
and if you don't..

00:02:45.946 --> 00:02:47.739
There's the charger.

00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:49.762
What's over here?

00:02:49.762 --> 00:02:50.595
Oooh!

00:02:54.565 --> 00:02:56.306
The Switch, essentially.

00:02:56.306 --> 00:02:58.048
Not really sure the technical names

00:02:58.048 --> 00:02:59.387
that they're calling everything,

00:02:59.387 --> 00:03:00.801
I probably should've looked that up,

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:03.636
but I would call this
the Switch converter.

00:03:03.636 --> 00:03:05.777
It essentially converts what is happening

00:03:05.777 --> 00:03:07.824
here on your little tablet.

00:03:07.824 --> 00:03:09.232
This plugs right into your TV

00:03:09.232 --> 00:03:13.313
and from there it switches tablet to TV.

00:03:13.313 --> 00:03:15.573
It's the switcher.

00:03:15.573 --> 00:03:16.708
Switch it up.

00:03:16.708 --> 00:03:20.840
Got your AC adapter here, USB, HDMI out,

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:22.737
and right inside here you can see

00:03:22.737 --> 00:03:25.568
there is a little
docking port right there.

00:03:25.568 --> 00:03:28.037
Ooh our other Joy-Con strap.

00:03:28.037 --> 00:03:29.709
This box is really pretty too.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.898
I kinda wanna save it.

00:03:31.898 --> 00:03:33.814
So to release these, you just have to

00:03:33.814 --> 00:03:36.659
push this little button
right here, pull up.

00:03:36.659 --> 00:03:41.492
And connecting the Joy-Cons
to the tablet, just as easy.

00:03:41.492 --> 00:03:44.075
(upbeat music)

00:03:45.261 --> 00:03:47.903
It feels pretty solid,

00:03:47.903 --> 00:03:50.320
it's a nice substantial feel.

00:03:54.299 --> 00:03:56.716
And there we go, switched in.

00:03:57.713 --> 00:04:00.137
I like how this kinda
hides all of the cords.

00:04:00.137 --> 00:04:02.507
So here it is, this is gonna
look really good in my office,

00:04:02.507 --> 00:04:04.311
I could also coordinate my lights

00:04:04.311 --> 00:04:06.632
to go with the colors of the controllers.

00:04:06.632 --> 00:04:10.147
So here's where the game card is inserted.

00:04:10.147 --> 00:04:12.395
Since we're here I guess we might as well,

00:04:12.395 --> 00:04:16.928
take a peek at what the
cartridge looks like.

00:04:16.928 --> 00:04:20.207
It's so little, it's like
the size of an SD card.

00:04:20.207 --> 00:04:23.040
Is it supposed to make that noise?

00:04:24.052 --> 00:04:26.969
It's got a real SD card feel to it.

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:31.903
And for a size comparison
of the little case.

00:04:31.903 --> 00:04:33.782
Not too much though. (giggles)

00:04:33.782 --> 00:04:35.055
It definitely is a little bit bigger.

00:04:35.055 --> 00:04:36.175
Well since we're here,

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:39.002
I might as well unbox
these Amiibo as well.

00:04:39.002 --> 00:04:41.222
Let's do Zelda first.

00:04:41.222 --> 00:04:43.424
(upbeat music)

00:04:43.424 --> 00:04:46.054
This is our Link Rider.

00:04:46.054 --> 00:04:47.622
Oh these look really good.

00:04:47.622 --> 00:04:49.622
The detail's incredible.

00:04:50.979 --> 00:04:52.977
This is probably the most
realistic I think of any..

00:04:52.977 --> 00:04:53.993
What's that little..?

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:57.474
Is this snow? Is that a little snowbank?

00:04:57.474 --> 00:05:00.057
(upbeat music)

00:05:04.947 --> 00:05:08.780
Oh great smell, a very
good smell to this guy.

00:05:10.025 --> 00:05:12.069
God, the detail, I just can't get over it.

00:05:12.069 --> 00:05:14.425
They did such a good job with these.

00:05:14.425 --> 00:05:15.876
I'm super impressed.

00:05:15.876 --> 00:05:17.095
Well I guess now it's time for

00:05:17.095 --> 00:05:22.095
a nice little slowmo video
montage of this sexy Switch.

00:05:22.113 --> 00:05:25.446
(calm electronic music)

00:06:22.083 --> 00:06:23.284
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:06:23.284 --> 00:06:24.581
I hope you guys enjoy this video.

00:06:24.581 --> 00:06:25.835
I'm super excited about the Switch

00:06:25.835 --> 00:06:27.862
and all of the games coming
out for it later this year.

00:06:27.862 --> 00:06:30.597
I'm gonna be posting a Nintendo
Switch setup in my office.

00:06:30.597 --> 00:06:32.193
So I'll be giving you a setup tour

00:06:32.193 --> 00:06:33.554
of where I'm gonna be setting it

00:06:33.554 --> 00:06:35.698
and a tour of sorta my gaming setup,

00:06:35.698 --> 00:06:38.002
which is directly behind
where I'm filming right now.

00:06:38.002 --> 00:06:41.648
See, the two cameras, two monitors,

00:06:41.648 --> 00:06:44.648
so I can see what I'm doing, office.

00:06:45.984 --> 00:06:48.791
All right, well that's it,
I'll see you guys soon, bye!

00:06:48.791 --> 00:06:50.428
I've messed things up in boxes before

00:06:50.428 --> 00:06:52.297
so there is a possibility
of messing this up.

00:06:52.297 --> 00:06:54.907
I mean nothing is ever guaranteed.

00:06:54.907 --> 00:06:56.799
That's causing a little bit of a back up.

00:06:56.799 --> 00:06:58.168
Oh God!

00:06:58.168 --> 00:07:01.668
(slowed) Back up. Oh God!

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:05.339
(laughter)

